TITLE='Authentic title "Last Big Wealth Opportunity For The Next 10 Years (or MUCH longer)" is a scarcity/urgency frame. The script argues that the March 2026 war-driven sell-off is a buying window, backed by historical recovery data. STRONG against the 10-peer cohort (3.30x) but TYPICAL on the 5-peer sensitivity check (1.91x), so the tier is unstable. The urgency framing ("last", "window closing") is a prediction the script itself disclaims ("I can\'t tell you where the market is in 6 months"). Association only.'
THUMB='Registered maxresdefault 1280x720 (HTTP 200, real image). White background. Left: the recurring cartoon man in a white shirt, worried, hand on chin, mouth open. Right: a heavy black headline "IT\'S TIME NOW!" with a curved arrow pointing down at a rising green curve from a green dot labelled "PROFIT" / "NOW" to a red dot labelled "2036", plus a larger green arrow. At 320x180 the headline and "2036" stay legible; "PROFIT" is small. The 10-year (2036) horizon matches the title\'s "next 10 years".'
SCRIPT='An urgency essay: two-investor 2009 parable ($18,000 vs $210,000); March 2026 context (Iran strikes, Hormuz, Brent $72 to $118, S&P -4.6% quarter, VIX, Fear & Greed); fear chain and stagflation bear case; 1970s vs today; RBC conflict data; Gulf War, Iraq 2003, WWII; bull/bear statistics and rolling returns; 2009 Amazon/Microsoft/Apple recoveries; 2020 COVID; loss aversion; Dalbar; JPMorgan best days; three-part framework (S&P ETF 40-50%, quality stocks, discipline); dollar safe haven; Goldman target; three options; close. Directly verified (FRED): Brent ~$72 pre-war and $118 on 2026-03-20; S&P Q1 -4.6%; 1975 unemployment 9%; dollar +2.7% in March. Wrong or overstated: VIX "mid-teens to over 35" (closes ~18-21 to 31); "today inflation 2.7%" and "unemployment 4.2%" (latest at upload 2.4% and 4.4%); 1974 "toward 14.5%" (1980 peak); "$450, not $676" impossible; guy one\'s $18,000 does not reproduce; "no manager has beaten it" false; dollar reserve share and Treasury size stale. Many 2026 claims SOURCE_UNAVAILABLE. Not personalised advice. The stored ending is complete.'
